  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-1).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs at the point $(4,1).$ However note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $1,$ including $-1$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1\\le y<1,$ which can also be written as  $-1\\le f(x)<1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
